--- Parity (web source is THE spec) ---
  The web source is a pure presentational leaf: `function LiveStateIndicators({ state }: { state:
  VehicleState })` rendering a `flex flex-wrap gap-2` of FIVE `<Badge variant dot size="lg">` chips, using
  `useTranslation` + `useUnits().formatSpeed`. Its parent (VehicleDetailPage.tsx) owns the `!state` skeleton
  and the `<SectionErrorBoundary>` failure. The native port reproduces the five chips + extends with the P4
  leaf contract (loading/empty/error + stale/offline) fed by the parent lifecycle.
  Data sources : useTranslation -> P1/S10 LiveStateIndicatorsStrings facade ; useUnits -> formatSpeed
                 reproduced via LiveStateFormat.speed (SI m/s → km/h·mph, convertSpeedFromSI +
                 Intl.NumberFormat grouping + half-away-from-zero, precision 0). No HTTP in the view — it
                 binds through LiveStateIndicatorsModel (P1/S8 seam).
  i18n keys    : the source routes ALL chip words through t(key, default) — 10 keys, reproduced verbatim:
                 common.speed/locked/unlocked/sentry/active/off/climate/on/charging/notCharging. Parity
                 check below = 10/10, 0 missing / 0 dead. Unit symbols (km/h, mph) are SI/scale literals.
  Badges       : (web source order, value + variant)
                 1 Speed   "{t('common.speed')}: {formatSpeed(state.speed,{precision:0})}" — success when
                           state.speed > 0 else neutral.
                 2 Lock    state.is_locked ? "Locked" : "Unlocked" — success when locked else DANGER.
                 3 Sentry  "{t('common.sentry')}: {state.sentry_mode ? 'Active' : 'Off'}" — warning when
                           armed else neutral.
                 4 Climate "{t('common.climate')}: {state.is_climate_on ? 'On' : 'Off'}" — info when on
                           else neutral.
                 5 Charging state.is_charging ? "Charging" : "Not Charging" — warning when charging else
                           neutral.
  Badge chrome : web `<Badge dot size="lg">` -> status dot (web `h-1.5 w-1.5 bg-current` = the tone colour)
                 + tone-tinted capsule (variant palette) + larger medium label (size lg = text-sm
                 font-medium). The dot is decorative; the combined text is the VoiceOver label; the chip is
                 static (web Badge is a <span>, not a control).
  Colour map   : ADR-006 semantic (not literal Tailwind) — success->statusSuccess, danger->statusDanger,
                 warning->statusWarning, info->statusInfo, neutral->textMuted.
  Layout       : web `flex flex-wrap gap-2` -> a SwiftUI Layout (LiveStateIndicatorsFlowLayout) that wraps
                 left-to-right with TSSpacing.sm gaps; tokens only, no Tailwind ports, no raw hex.

